---
import Breadcrumb from "../components/Breadcrumb.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../config/site";
import { webPageJsonLd } from "../lib/seo";

const title = "Contact | Yardwork";
const description =
  "Contact Yardwork Calculators. The email and mailing address on this page are placeholders until the site is published.";
const pathname = "/contact/";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={webPageJsonLd(title, description, pathname)}>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <Breadcrumb current="Contact" />
    <h1>Contact</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Corrections to a formula or a density, and questions about the site, can come here once the
      placeholder below has been replaced.
    </p>
  </header>
  <article class="prose">
    <div class="todo-banner">
      <p>
        <strong>TODO:</strong> This contact information is a placeholder. Replace the email and mailing
        address before you publish the site or apply for AdSense. Both values live in one file,
        <code>src/config/site.ts</code>, next to the site URL.
      </p>
    </div>
    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>
    </p>
    <h2>Mail</h2>
    <p>{site.contact.mailingAddress}</p>
    <h2>What is worth writing about</h2>
    <p>
      A supplier density that should be added, a bag size that is now the common one in stores, or
      a result that does not match the working on the page. Include the page address and the
      numbers you typed. The calculators do not store what you entered, so the message has to
      carry the example.
    </p>
    <p>
      There is no phone number yet, and there is no contact form, because a form would need a
      mailbox that is actually delivered. Until the TODO above is resolved, do not treat the
      example.com address as a way to reach anyone.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
